          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "intersection is referred to in the following manner: If the second street running in the N–S direction and 5th street in the E–W direction meet at some crossing, then we call this street intersection (2, 5). Using this convention, find:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.23,
            0.194,
            0.883,
            0.215
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(a) how many street intersections can be referred to as (4, 3)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.229,
            0.218,
            0.883,
            0.239
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(b) how many street intersections can be referred to as (3, 4)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.134,
            0.248,
            0.886,
            0.371
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "15. A computer graphics program displays images on a rectangular screen whose coordinate system has the origin at the bottom-left corner. The screen is 800 pixels wide and 600 pixels high. A circular icon of radius 80 pixels is drawn with its centre at the point A (100, 150). Another circular icon of radius 100 pixels is drawn with its centre at the point B (250, 230). Determine:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.182,
            0.374,
            0.835,
            0.395
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) whether any part of either circle lies outside the screen."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.182,
            0.399,
            0.712,
            0.42
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) whether the two circles intersect each other."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.135,
            0.428,
            0.886,
            0.491
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "16. Plot the points A (2, 1), B (–1, 2), C (–2, –1), and D (1, –2) in the coordinate plane. Is ABCD a square? Can you explain why? What is the area of this square?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.37,
            0.507,
            0.63,
            0.529
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Chapter Summary"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.158,
            0.549,
            0.886,
            0.611
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "z To locate the position of an object or a point in a plane, we require two perpendicular lines — One of them is horizontal, and the other is vertical."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.158,
            0.619,
            0.886,
            0.662
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "z The plane is called the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "cartesian plane",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ", the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "coordinate plane",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " or the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "xy-plane",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and the lines are called the coordinate axes."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.159,
            0.669,
            0.886,
            0.71
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "z The horizontal line is called the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "x-axis",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and the vertical line is called the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "y-axis",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.159,
            0.719,
            0.885,
            0.76
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "z The coordinate axes divide the plane into four parts called "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "quadrants",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.159,
            0.768,
            0.791,
            0.79
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "z The point of intersection of the axes is called the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "origin",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.159,
            0.797,
            0.886,
            0.88
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "z The distance of a point from the y-axis is its "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "x-coordinate",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and the distance of the point from the x-axis is its "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "y-coordinate",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". If the x-coordinate of a point is x, and the y-coordinate is y, then (x, y) are called the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "coordinates",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " of the point."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
